<article class="env-proposition" id="9FABF2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9FABF2">Proposition <span data-tag="9FABF2">1.2.5.1</span> <span class="named">(Joyal <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/joyalpub">joyalpub</a>]</span>)</span>.</a>$\infty $-groupoid Let $\calC $ be a simplicial set. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The simplicial set $\calC $ is an $\infty $-category and its homotopy category $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ is a groupoid. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The simplicial set $\calC $ satisfies the extension condition for all horn inclusions $\Lambda ^ n_ i \subseteq \Delta ^ n$ for $0 \leq i < n$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
The simplicial set $\calC $ satisfies the extension condition for all horn inclusions $\Lambda ^ n_ i \subseteq \Delta ^ n$ for $0 < i \leq n$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
The simplicial set $\calC $ is a Kan complex; in other words, it satisfies the extension condition for all horn inclusions $\Lambda ^ n_ i \subseteq \Delta ^ n$ for $0 \leq i \leq n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The equivalence $(1) \Leftrightarrow (2)$ follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/BC1240" data-tag="BC1240">1.2.4.3</a>. Similarly, the equivalence $(1) \Leftrightarrow (3)$ follows by applying Proposition <a href="/tag/BC1240" data-tag="BC1240">1.2.4.3</a> to $\calC ^{op}$. We conclude by observing that $(4) \Leftrightarrow (2) \wedge (3)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>